Z||000000||MEC91Firebird||02-11-2001||12:20 AM||||I got a ticket yesterday, 51 in a 35.  It was my fault, but i thought i was in a 45, of all the times I speed around, i get caught when I  THOUGHT I was doing close to the right speed!!   Ugh, I am soooo unhappy, just had to let someone know.||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||02-11-2001||12:26 AM||||even if it was a 45, you were still speeding  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>my dad got pulled over once for doing 39 in a 35, and it was where the speed limit was going up to 45. cop musta been having a sh!tty day or something.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||02-11-2001||01:15 AM||||My last speeding ticket was in 1986 and I got nailed for the same reason.  Country road, late at night, very dark, speed limit signs hidden among the tree branches (really!) and I'm going 61 so I figure just about 5mph over.  Police car pulls out from hiding and turns the lights on.  I'm thinking big deal, I'll just get a warning.  Says it's a 35mph zone.  WHAT????  Really ticked me off.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||02-11-2001||02:00 AM||||I got polled over once for doing 54 in a 25.<BR>It was a dirt road that parallels the main road into town. Well, apparantly with no signs the dirt road becomes a residential zone when it enters town. After a week of driving that route and not knowing. Some lady called the cops and they set up a speed trap. Since there wasn't a sign I only got a warning, but I still go by the lady's house at 55 because it's out of town. (But not lately because my Fiero gets dirty enough driving down paved roads.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||02-11-2001||08:38 AM||||The other night on one of those police chase shows they had some guy blow by a police car(that was cruising on patrol) on a major highway very early in the morning when there was no traffic at about 120 MPH.He never even saw the cop car.when the cop caught him he didn't ticket him.He took him away in handcuffs.<BR> <BR>             ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||02-11-2001||09:52 AM||||Hugh, I saw that, too. Guy was driving a Mustang. Looked like he nearly blew the paint off the cop car when he went past! <BR>My last ticket was about three years ago. 72 in a 50. What really ticked me off was that this was about 2:00 AM, and there was nearly no traffic. I drive the same section of road every day, coming home from work, and it's 70-75 MPH, bumper to bumper, and there's not a cop in sight. It just isn't enforced. <BR>Cop was really nervous, too. When he pulled over a lowered black Sonoma with tinted windows flying low at 2:00 AM, I think he expected to see someone much more sinister than me!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||02-11-2001||10:09 PM||||Ticket stories... yay!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Last Monday I was pulled over by a detective in an unmarked car while I was speeding to get to class.  He said I was doing 45 in a 25... which I was how fast I was going down my street.  The problem was that it took him till I was already at the college (ten minutes from my house) before he was close enough to pull me over.  Doh!  Luckily he saw my F.O.P card and said "Have a nice day and slow down".  Nicest guy I ever had pull me over.<P>The time I got pulled over before that was in my first Fiero... 60 in the park (30mph zone)... the ranger was not too happy about that one.  But, my old F.O.P. card saved the day.  (The ranger did rip that one up though.  And the one I have now is from '99... I'm pushing my luck with these things.)<P>But since Monday... I find myself doing no more than 5mph over the speed limit... the unmarked car did the trick I guess.||||reg||1
